Reporting to the Vice President of Revenue Cycle, the Revenue Cycle Manager will provide leadership over the day-to-day and strategic operations of the Revenue Cycle Management (RCM) department.
The Revenue Cycle Manager is required to have demonstrated advanced knowledge and understanding of all aspects of billing office operations, including principles of staff management/supervision;
office workflows;
Collaborates with affiliates, providers if needed, and the central business office on process improvement opportunities.
Conduct weekly meetings with the RCM team to provide guidance and feedback
Champions the effectiveness of revenue cycle functional team efforts and recommends improvement strategies to enhance overall efficiency across remote teams
Bachelor’s degree in Health Care Management or Administration, or a related field, five to seven years of medical billing office experience, of which at least four years were at the management level or equivalent combination of education and/or experience
HFMA Certified Revenue Cycle Representative (CRCR) or must obtain certification in the first 6-months of employment
Proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.)
Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to build relationships with team members
